The product name in the settings folder and the settings files' comments comes from PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME (default
"Project Helghast", so Project Helghast builds are unchanged). Carried KZ3 patches 2037/2095/2103/4028 hard-code their
own name: cellPad.c makes %APPDATA%\Project Helghast for keybinds.ini (and display.ini, which the port puts beside it),
and pad_keybinds.h / rsx_display_mode.h write "# Project Helghast ..." comments. A second port built from the same
series then wrote its settings into the other project's folder under the other project's name. R&C sets
PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME to "Qwark's Awakening" in port/rc/CMakeLists.txt (PUBLIC on ps3recomp_runtime, so main.cpp's
display.ini writer gets it too). R&C, 2026-11-02.

--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -268,7 +268,7 @@
  * alongside an XInput pad on port 0 (buttons OR'ed, a key-held stick direction overrides that stick). The file is
  * keybinds.ini in the player's data folder, the same folder tools/release/launch.py data_dir() picks: the install
  * folder when kz3-install.ini (next to the exe or one level up, <root>/build/kz3.exe) says [install] portable = 1,
- * else %APPDATA%\Project Helghast. KZ3_KEYBINDS=<path> names another file (tests). Missing = written with the
+ * else %APPDATA%\<PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME> (R&C patch 6010; default Project Helghast). KZ3_KEYBINDS=<path> names another file (tests). Missing = written with the
  * defaults; re-read when its time stamp changes (checked every 2 s). Parser, defaults, writer: pad_keybinds.h. */
 #include "pad_keybinds.h"
 #include "pad_dsu_io.h"   /* KZ3 patch 4028: DSU motion client */
@@ -434,7 +434,7 @@
     n = GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"APPDATA", appdata, 1024);
     if (n > 0 && n < 1000) {
         wchar_t dir[1024];
